FORMAT 1
SCENARIO My first repository
LABEL    Worksheet 1
SUMMARY  Git setup, git init, add, commit – the first version of a recipe.
INTRO    You are **Jana Nováková** at a school computer. Follow the tasks; each one is ticked off automatically once you complete it.
INTRO    It is about the steps, not about typing: where there would be a lot to type, the simulator fills in part of it and tells you (in violet).

SETUP
  PERSON jana NAME "Jana Nováková" EMAIL "novakovaj@jirovcovka.net" LOGIN "jana-novakova" LABEL "Jana's computer"
  MACHINE jana
  REPOSITORY git/cookbook
END

TASK Find out which folder you are in and which version of Git you have.
  HINT  pwd
  HINT  git --version
  CHECK command "pwd" was run
  CHECK command "git --version" was run
END

TASK Set your name. The simulator fills in the rest of the setup. Then list the whole setup.
  HINT     git config --global user.name "Jana Nováková"
  HINT     git config --global --list
  QUESTION Which lines did the simulator fill in? Why will you type them yourself at school?
  CHECK    config user.name is set
  CHECK    command "git config --global --list" was run after command "git config --global user.name..."
  AUTO WHEN config user.name is set
    NOTE five more setup lines – your school e-mail (the same as on GitHub), the default branch `main`, VS Code as the editor, `git pull` with merging, and accented characters in file names. At school you will type them yourself.
    PS> git config --global user.email "novakovaj@jirovcovka.net"
    PS> git config --global init.defaultBranch main
    PS> git config --global core.editor "code --wait"
    PS> git config --global pull.rebase false
    PS> git config --global core.quotepath false
  END
END

TASK Create a folder **git** and inside it **cookbook**. Open it in VS Code and turn it into a repository.
  HINT     cd ~
  HINT     mkdir git
  HINT     cd git
  HINT     mkdir cookbook
  HINT     cd cookbook
  HINT     code -r .
  HINT     git init
  HINT     git status
  QUESTION What did git status say on its last line?
  CHECK    repository exists
  CHECK    vscode folder is git/cookbook
  CHECK    command "git status" was run
END

TASK In the Explorer, create a file **pancakes.md** with a heading `#` and a subheading `##`. Save it (**Ctrl+S**) and look at the preview. The simulator fills in the ingredients. Then run `git status`.
  NOTE     Click the **+** icon above the file list and type:
  HINT     # Pancakes
  HINT
  HINT     ## Ingredients
  QUESTION What colour is the file name and under which heading is it?
  CHECK    file pancakes.md contains line starting with "# "
  CHECK    file pancakes.md contains line starting with "## "
  CHECK    output of "git status" contains "Untracked files"
  CHECK    output of "git status" contains "pancakes.md"
  AUTO WHEN file pancakes.md contains line starting with "## "
    NOTE the ingredients as bullet points (lines starting with `- `). See how they look in the preview.
    APPEND pancakes.md

      - 250 ml milk
      - 1 egg
      - 120 g plain flour
      - a pinch of salt
    END
  END
END

TASK Make your first commit.
  NOTE     You can write the commit message your own way, as long as it is clear.
  HINT     git add pancakes.md
  HINT     git status
  HINT     git commit -m "Add pancake recipe"
  QUESTION What colour is the file after git add? What does -m mean?
  CHECK    file pancakes.md in HEAD exists
END

TASK Add a subheading `## Tip` at the end of the recipe and save – the simulator adds a sentence below it. Then make a second commit.
  HINT  ## Tip
  HINT
  HINT  git add pancakes.md
  HINT  git commit -m "Add filling tip"
  CHECK commit count is at least 2
  CHECK file pancakes.md in HEAD contains line starting with "## Tip"
  AUTO WHEN file pancakes.md contains line starting with "## Tip"
    NOTE one sentence under the tip. Words between asterisks are shown in *italics* in the preview.
    APPEND pancakes.md

      I fill them with *strawberry jam*.
    END
  END
END

TASK Look at the history.
  HINT  git log --oneline
  CHECK command "git log..." was run
  CHECK commit count is at least 2
END
